      "Building the massive data centers required for artificial intelligence is fantastically expensive. It’s a capital black hole that has spooked investors, even sparking lawsuits alleging Oracle tried to hide the “massive increases in CapEx” from the market. The fear is simple: spending billions on infrastructure today for revenue that might show up tomorrow is a great way to destroy value.",
